hub.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":8,"closed_issues":4466,"state":"closed","created_at":"2024-02-14T11:52:07Z","updated_at":"2026-10-05T23:48:31Z","due_on":"2025-03-03T00:00:00Z","closed_at":"2025-03-19T09:35:35Z"},"comments":8,"created_at":"2024-10-23T03:26:39Z","updated_at":"2026-06-26T16:50:46Z","closed_at":"2024-11-12T15:36:09Z","assignee":{"login":"SaracenOne","id":12756047,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzU2MDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12756047?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SaracenOne","html_url":"https://github.com/SaracenOne","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SaracenOne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SaracenOne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SaracenOne/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SaracenOne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SaracenOne/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SaracenOne/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SaracenOne/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SaracenOne/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SaracenOne/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/98446","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98446","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98446.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98446.patch","merged_at":"2024-11-12T15:36:09Z"},"body":"Add a LookAtModifier3D. This modifier allows you to specify a forward axis and provides a two-axis Euler rotation to prevent roll the forward axis.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/33486536-142f-406a-b310-cb1d62c9c887\r\n\r\n- Follow up https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/87888\r\n\r\n# Features\r\n\r\n## Time-based interpolation\r\n\r\nWhen the character changes the lock-on target, it will take a certain amount of time to rotate instead of immediately rotating its head. The time-based interpolation uses a tween, so several transition/easing types can be selected.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f0e18406-2be9-4695-92bf-aba8005cf7e6\r\n\r\n## Angle limitation\r\n\r\nThis option allows you to prevent the character's neck from rotating 360 degrees. The limitation means that half angle of the limit from the bone rest is the range of motion. Both symmetrical and non-symmetrical limitations are supported.\r\n\r\nAlso, when this option is enabled, time-based interpolation will provide rest-aware rotation, similar to AnimationTree blending. This means that in some cases the shortest path will not be selected to prevent bones from penetrating through the body. See also [for-better-blending](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/animation/animation_tree.html#for-better-blending).\r\n\r\nIn addition, if the target moves outside of these limits, axis flipping may occur, where time-based interpolation is used.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/056b9503-cd11-4576-9148-7e160a84cab3\r\n\r\n## Non-linear damping\r\n\r\nTo prevent abrupt changes in angular velocity at the edge of the angular limit, the option is to start non-linear(b-spline) damping from the threshold value.\r\n\r\nThis helps simulate natural human motion.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/10696033-0d39-42a7-b5f4-8a23872e90fa\r\n\r\n## Origin setting\r\n\r\nThere are some cases where multiple bones need to always point in the same direction, such as the eyes.\r\n\r\nFor example, angle limitation may cause bone to flip outside their limits, which is not good because only one of the eyes will move significantly. Setting an arbitrary origin helps to solve this problem.\r\n\r\n### Origin from\r\n\r\nFor example, To solve the above problem, it is possible to set the head to origin for eyes. Or you can use BoneAttachment or parent-child Node3D.\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5d35fac5-1cff-4554-99d9-a9b562f98413)\r\n\r\n### Offset\r\n\r\nThe problem can be addressed by matching the origin by offset without any external node or bone as well.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/95d55acd-d140-415a-8287-f93e03ff5c10\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98446/reactions","total_count":100,"+1":23,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":34,"confused":0,"heart":30,"rocket":0,"eyes":13},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98446/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}